FUN_0000_ab03 (per-object animation-frame UPDATE method, dispatched by 7c1d's CS-table1, patch 244):
object + indexed-table + sub-dispatch base-loss (SIGSEGV) and WORD-width bugs.

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0xab03-0xab81; gdb crash reading [di+0x42] with
di=near-offset 0x C05C as a host pointer).  ab03 is one of 7c1d's table1 entries; c0e5/7c1d dispatch it
with di (the object near-offset) in arg0.  Ghidra treated di as a host pointer for every [di+off] field,
base-lost the DS-relative indexed table read (word[DS:byte[di+0x1b]*2-0x7a60]) and the two frame
sub-dispatch tables (near call word[DS:idx-0x6704 / idx-0x6724], idx=(byte[di+0x42]&0xf)*2), and read
the position-history rotation (0x26..0x2e) as 4-byte int where the asm is movswl (WORD sign-extend) /
WORD store.  Fix: object = g_mem+0x1c000+di; rebase the object fields + the -0x7a60 read + the two
sub-dispatch table reads to the DGROUP base; WORD widths for the rotation; sub-dispatch targets called
near with di live.  The DAT_2000_* accessors (5a08/578c/578a/5796/5798/3d2a/3ae0) are already correctly
resolved (0x2000-base offset == 0x1c00:off) and stay verbatim.  Mission-cascade only.
